      "summary": ": Today's Ski Summary Wednesday, August 12, 2026 – 4:55 AM NZST Cardrona is open today, though strong northerly winds are impacting lift operations across the mountain. The grooming team took full advantage of a clear overnight freeze to lay down crisp corduroy across open terrain, while off-piste areas start firm before softening down low as temperatures rise. Snow showers are expected to develop mid-day alongside building winds, so visitors should bring snow chains as road requirements can change at any time. Main Basin lifts are scheduled to turn from 8:30 AM, with Captain's Express, the T-Bar, and Willows Chair scheduled to follow (though some lifts will experience wind holds depending on exposure). Terrain is 7/10 open, including the Learners Slope, Main Basin, Captain's Basin, Little Willows, Big Willows, Arcadia Chutes, and Ski Touring Access. Mt Cardrona and Summit are currently on hold due to wind, while Soho is closed for the day (from 11:30 AM) due to incoming weather conditions.",
